  "final_message": "The bug is fixed and `test_public.py` passes (1/1).\n\nThe problem was that `add_tag` used `tags=[]` as its default. Python creates that default list once and reuses it for every call, so tags from one call showed up in later, unrelated calls. The default is now `tags=None`, and the function creates a new empty list when `tags` isn't given.\n\nWhen a caller passes their own `tags` list, it's still used as given: in a quick check, the record's `tags` was that same list object, with the new tag appended. `remove_tag` is unchanged.\n\nDONE: Fixed the shared mutable default in `add_tag` (`tags=None` plus a new list per call); test passes and caller-supplied lists are still used as given.",
